  - m_Id: 27156260410605568
    m_Localized: Patch Notes
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28354470692401152
    m_Localized: "Patch Notes\n1. Gameplay Systems\n1.1. The plant growing system
      has been reworked\n1.2. Shelf placement and usage logic has been updated\n1.3.
      Products no longer require individual shelves. After placing a shelf, you can
      choose which products will be stored on it\n1.4. Selected products on shelves
      are now saved\n1.5. The garden bed system has been reworked: beds and seeds
      are purchased separately, after which you can choose which plant to grow\n1.6.
      Plants are now divided into types. Each type can only be grown on the corresponding
      bed\n1.7. Object settings are now preserved when moving the object\n1.8. A
      new type of interactive object has been added \u2014 interaction now requires
      a button press\n1.9. A notice board has been added\n\n2. Balance & Economy\n2.1.
      Product prices have been updated\n\n3. Visual Changes\n\n3.1. Updated icons
      for plants, products, and beds\n3.2. Updated bed visuals\n\n4. Audio\n4.1.
      Footstep sounds have been balanced\n4.2. Checkout scanner sound volume has
      been reduced"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28379935339589632
    m_Localized: Upcoming Changes
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28556219701297152
    m_Localized: "1. Radio\nRadio will appear in the game. It can be turned on to
      listen to music and informational broadcasts.\n2. Plant watering system\nPlants
      will need to be watered periodically. Without watering their growth will slow
      down or stop completely.\n3. Compost pit\nA system for processing products
      and organic waste into compost will be added.\n4. Bed fertilizing system\nBeds
      can be fertilized with compost. Without fertilization plants will eventually
      stop growing.\n5. Technical interface improvements\nInternal improvements to
      the UI system will be implemented. They will not change gameplay but will speed
      up further development and improve interface stability.\n6. Production zone\nA
      production processing zone will be added. For example vegetables and fruits
      can be processed into new products (for example carrot \u2192 carrot juice).\n7.
      Changing the size of game zones\nA system for changing the size of zones using
      neighboring territories will appear.\n8. New game zones\nNew functional zones
      are planned:\n8.1. restaurant\n8.2. kitchen\n8.3. warehouse\n\nYou can suggest
      ideas for future updates or report bugs in the game comments or in the Telegram
      channel: t.me/MoodyDustGames"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
